  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \nWell above normal temperatures again today with light winds across\nthe region. \n\nBy Friday, an upper level trough across the northwest CONUS will \npush southeast through the western states and will begin to move a \nmuch cooler air mass into the intermountain west behind a strong \ncold front. As the trough pushes southeast, southwesterly winds will \nbegin to increase, with speeds reaching 15-20 mph and gusts up to 25-\n30 mph on Friday. Conditions remain dry as little moisture will be \npresent over Nevada. Concurrently, as the low pressure pushes \nsoutheast, remnants from Hurricane Rachel will push northward into \nsouthern Nevada, getting absorbed into the mean upper level flow, \nand bring a big increase in moisture.\n\nChances for showers increase Saturday and will persist through \nWednesday, with the highest chances (40-60%) expected on both Sunday \nand Monday. Though Sunday is expected to see the greatest amount of \naccumulating precipitation. Temperatures will see a big dip as the \ncold front moves over Nevada Friday night-Saturday morning with \nhighs in the 80s on Friday, and dropping into the 70s Saturday. By \nSunday, temperatures expected to see another dip with highs only in \nthe 50s across northern Nevada, 60s in central Nevada. Overnight \nlows will also see a drop in temperatures starting in the 40s on \nFriday, and reaching to freezing temperatures in the 20s and 30s by \nSunday lasting through Wednesday. Chances for snow return in the \nforecast each night however snow amounts are very low and are \nexpected to remain in the mountain peaks as snow levels drop slowly \neach day staying above 8000 feet. Breezy southerly winds Saturday \nthrough Monday with speeds up to 20-25 mph, gusts up to 35-45 mph \nwith strongest winds on Saturday in central Nevada.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence for dry and\nabove normal temperatures today and tomorrow. High confidence for\na low pressure system moving into Nevada late Friday and over the\nweekend. High confidence of gusty winds increasing Friday with\nstronger winds on Saturday. Moderate confidence in regards to \nmoisture from a Pacific tropical storm moving into Nevada over the\nweekend bringing in increasing chances for showers. High\nconfidence in regards to much cooler temperatures moving into\nnorthern and central Nevada over the weekend. Moderate confidence\nin regards to precipitation over the weekend and lasting through \nnext week. Low confidence in regards to mountain snow over the \nweekend. Changes to wind gusts in the grids to better represent\nthe increasing wind speeds Friday.",
